================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

TRACE builds on prior open-source work rather than reimplementing solved
problems. The projects below are used as libraries and/or as direct technical
references. All are MIT or MIT/Apache-2.0 licensed, which permits commercial
use with attribution.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Handy — https://github.com/cjpais/Handy
MIT License. Copyright (c) Handy contributors.

Used as a technical reference for the Tauri 2 + Rust + React architecture,
the audio/transcription module boundaries, typed IPC via specta, and local
model management. TRACE does not fork or vendor Handy's code; it is a
different product (meeting capture, not push-to-talk dictation).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
transcribe-rs — https://crates.io/crates/transcribe-rs
MIT License. Copyright (c) CJ Pais.

Used as a library. Provides the unified `SpeechModel` interface over Parakeet,
Whisper and other ONNX/GGML engines, which is the TranscriptionProvider
abstraction TRACE's specs called for.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
cpal — https://github.com/RustAudio/cpal
Apache-2.0 License.

Used as a library for cross-platform microphone capture.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
wasapi-rs — https://github.com/HEnquist/wasapi-rs
MIT License. Copyright (c) Henrik Enquist.

Used as a library for Windows system-audio loopback capture. cpal does not
support WASAPI loopback (see RustAudio/cpal#476), so this is used directly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Voicebox — https://github.com/jamiepine/voicebox
MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 Voicebox Contributors.

Its tauri/src-tauri/src/audio_capture/ module is the reference and basis for
TRACE's system-audio capture: WASAPI loopback on Windows (windows.rs) and
ScreenCaptureKit on macOS (macos.rs). TRACE adapts the capture approach and the
COM-threading pattern rather than vendoring the files, and replaces its
unbounded sample buffer with a bounded ring buffer suitable for long meetings.

No other part of Voicebox is used. It is a voice-studio application with a
Python/FastAPI backend, which TRACE deliberately does not adopt.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
heed — https://github.com/isjunrod/heed
MIT License.

Architectural reference only; no code used. Independently validated the
dual-channel microphone/system-audio separation and the live-pass plus
accurate-re-pass transcription design.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MeetingBro — https://github.com/armpro24-blip/MeetingBro
MIT License.

Behavioural reference only; no code used. Confirmed device-level WASAPI
loopback as the correct Windows system-audio approach.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Models

Speech recognition uses NVIDIA Parakeet models, distributed under their own
licence terms from NVIDIA / Hugging Face. Local language models are supplied
by the user's own Ollama installation and are subject to each model's licence.
No model weights are bundled with TRACE; all are downloaded on first run.
